{
  // A tenant's life, and the three points something can be told about.
  //
  // Written as a flow — nodes and links — because that is what it is. The
  // first draft drew the same figure as a grid with spacer cells and hand
  // placed line elements, which is how you build a flow when you have not
  // read that the compiler has one.
  //
  // The three points are drawn as the stages they are, because that is the
  // claim: they are moments in the tenant's own coming-up, not a mechanism
  // beside it.
  //
  // It draws the coming-up and nothing else. A first version carried the two
  // ways out as well and came to eleven hundred points wide on a page that is
  // seven hundred and sixty — a flow lays its nodes on one rank, so branching
  // makes it wider rather than taller. The prose says what a changed or
  // removed declaration does, and says it better than two more boxes would.

  // Lini's own default stroke is a THREE-digit hex pair, and a three-digit
  // hex is indistinguishable from an issue reference to the branding ratchet.
  // Stating the colour at full length keeps the check honest rather than
  // loosened; dbo.css maps --lini-* onto the site palette either way.
  --stroke: #444444;
  --accent: #a8641b; --accent-soft: #f6efe4;
  --seal: #14532d;   --seal-soft: #e7f0e9;
  --faint: #8695a3;  --line: #e3e0da;      --bg: #fbfaf8;
  font-family: "Google Sans"; font-size: 13;

  |point::box| { fill: --accent-soft; stroke: --accent; }
  |done::box|  { fill: --seal-soft; stroke: --seal; }
  |gone::box|  { fill: none; stroke: --line; stroke-style: dashed;
                 color: --faint; }
}

|box#declared|    "a declaration\nappears"
|box#provisioned| "provisioned"
|point#dispatch|  "dispatch"
|point#surfaces|  "surfaces"
|done#serving|    "serving"

declared -> provisioned -> dispatch -> surfaces -> serving
